{"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI","doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/ModifiedContent"]]},"sections":[],"metadata":{"extendedModule":"OpenSwiftUI","externalID":"s:11OpenSwiftUI5ScenePAAE22defaultWindowPlacementyQrAA0fG0VAA0F10LayoutRootV_AA0fG7ContextVtcF::SYNTHESIZED::s:11OpenSwiftUI15ModifiedContentV","symbolKind":"method","role":"symbol","modules":[{"name":"OpenSwiftUI"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"defaultWindowPlacement"},{"kind":"text","text":"(("},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"WindowLayoutRoot","preciseIdentifier":"s:11OpenSwiftUI16WindowLayoutRootV"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"WindowPlacementContext","preciseIdentifier":"s:11OpenSwiftUI22WindowPlacementContextV"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"WindowPlacement","preciseIdentifier":"s:11OpenSwiftUI15WindowPlacementV"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"some"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Scene","preciseIdentifier":"s:11OpenSwiftUI5SceneP"}],"title":"defaultWindowPlacement(_:)","roleHeading":"Instance Method"},"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"kind":"attribute","text":"@"},{"kind":"attribute","preciseIdentifier":"s:ScM","text":"MainActor"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"defaultWindowPlacement"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"_"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"internalParam","text":"makePlacement"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"attribute","text":"@escaping "},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/WindowLayoutRoot","preciseIdentifier":"s:11OpenSwiftUI16WindowLayoutRootV","text":"WindowLayoutRoot"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/WindowPlacementContext","preciseIdentifier":"s:11OpenSwiftUI22WindowPlacementContextV","text":"WindowPlacementContext"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/WindowPlacement","preciseIdentifier":"s:11OpenSwiftUI15WindowPlacementV","text":"WindowPlacement"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"some"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/Scene","preciseIdentifier":"s:11OpenSwiftUI5SceneP","text":"Scene"},{"kind":"text","text":"\n"}],"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["macOS"]}]},{"kind":"parameters","parameters":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A closure to generate the default window placement.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"name":"makePlacement"}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"anchor":"discussion","type":"heading","text":"Discussion"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Use this scene modifier to indicate a default initial size and position"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"for a new window that the system creates from a "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/Scene","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" declaration."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"On Windows, you can use the screen’s bounds to place the window."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"For example, you can specify that the window is always placed 140"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"points from the bottom of the screen:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":null,"code":["struct MyApp: App {","    var body: some Scene {","        ...","","        Window(\"Status\", id: \"status\") {","            StatusView()","        }","        .windowResizability(.contentSize)","        .defaultWindowPlacement { content, context in","            let displayBounds = context.defaultDisplay.visibleRect","            let size = content.sizeThatFits(.unspecified)","            let position = CGPoint(","                x: displayBounds.midX - (size.width \/ 2),","                y: displayBounds.maxY - size.height - 140)","            return WindowPlacement(position: position, size: size)","        }","    }","}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"On visionOS, the system always places the first window"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"relative to where the person is looking."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"The system ignores calls to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"defaultWindowPlacement(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"You can place any subsequent windows relative to existing ones by"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"returning one of the methods defined by "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"WindowPlacement\/Position"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"with the existing window."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"For example, you can align the new window with the trailing edge of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Content"},{"type":"text","text":" window:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":null,"code":["struct MyApp: App {","    @Environment(\\.openWindow) private var openWindow","","    var body: some Scene {","        WindowGroup(\"Content\", id: \"content\") {","            Button(\"Open status window\") {","                openWindow(id: \"status\")","            }","        }","","        WindowGroup(\"Status\", id: \"status\") {","            StatusView()","        }","        .windowResizability(.contentSize)","        .defaultWindowPlacement { content, context in","            if let contentWindow = context.windows.first(","            where: { $0.id == \"content\" }) {","                WindowPlacement(.trailing(contentWindow))","            } else {","                WindowPlacement()","            }","        }","    }","}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The placement that your function returns acts as a default for when the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"window first appears. People can later resize and move the window using"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"interface controls that the system provides. Also, during state"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"restoration, the system restores the window to it’s most recent size and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"position, rather than the default placement."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"For more information on configuring how scenes behave with"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"state restoration, see "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Scene.stateRestoration(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}]}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/openswiftui\/modifiedcontent\/defaultwindowplacement(_:)"]}],"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Defines a function used for determining the default placement"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"of windows."}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/ModifiedContent\/defaultWindowPlacement(_:)","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"references":{"doc://OpenSwiftUI/documentation/OpenSwiftUI/WindowLayoutRoot":{"url":"\/documentation\/openswiftui\/windowlayoutroot","identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/WindowLayoutRoot","title":"WindowLayoutRoot","role":"symbol","type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"A proxy which represents the root contents of a window.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"WindowLayoutRoot","kind":"identifier"}],"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"WindowLayoutRoot","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://OpenSwiftUI/documentation/OpenSwiftUI/WindowPlacement":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"WindowPlacement"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/WindowPlacement","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A type which represents a preferred size and position for a window."}],"title":"WindowPlacement","url":"\/documentation\/openswiftui\/windowplacement","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"WindowPlacement"}],"type":"topic"},"doc://OpenSwiftUI/documentation/OpenSwiftUI":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI","role":"collection","abstract":[],"title":"OpenSwiftUI","url":"\/documentation\/openswiftui","kind":"symbol","type":"topic"},"doc://OpenSwiftUI/documentation/OpenSwiftUI/ModifiedContent/defaultWindowPlacement(_:)":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/ModifiedContent\/defaultWindowPlacement(_:)","url":"\/documentation\/openswiftui\/modifiedcontent\/defaultwindowplacement(_:)","title":"defaultWindowPlacement(_:)","role":"symbol","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Defines a function used for determining the default placement"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"of windows."}],"fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"defaultWindowPlacement","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"((","kind":"text"},{"text":"WindowLayoutRoot","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:11OpenSwiftUI16WindowLayoutRootV"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"WindowPlacementContext","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:11OpenSwiftUI22WindowPlacementContextV"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"WindowPlacement","kind":"type